# 2026-08-04 (same session, forensic root-cause investigation after the
# Owner reported real WhatsApp/web failures post-restart): full read-only
# trace of 4 real Admin WhatsApp messages plus DB/log forensics found three
# distinct, evidenced root causes, fixed with Owner's directive to
# investigate-then-fix-minimally (no separate approval round requested for
# each -- directive pre-authorized fixes conditioned on root-cause proof):
#   1. AI_SAFE_MODE (and the rest of the customer-facing draft/safety
#      cascade) was incorrectly applying to Admin<->Hermes replies --
#      modules/bridge_poller/__init__.py now sends admin-role replies
#      directly, bypassing that cascade; the cascade itself is unchanged
#      for external/customer replies (additive if-branch, verified via
#      source-order regression test).
#   2. cash_ledger_summary (BUS-006) had no exact_answer template, so real
#      tool data fell through to a generic LLM chat-completion that ignored
#      it in favor of irrelevant RAG text -- modules/ai_console/
#      provider_registry.py now reuses the tool's own pre-computed
#      data["answer"] field, matching the existing pattern for 3 other
#      tools.
#   3. get_daily_payments()/get_employee_month_payments() in
#      modules/ai_readonly_tools/__init__.py queried fpe_cash_transactions
#      directly with a bad column reference (fpe_employees.employee_id
#      doesn't exist, real PK is .id -- confirmed via the actual FK
#      constraint) AND the fazle_ai_reader role production actually uses
#      has no SELECT grant on that raw table at all (confirmed via
#      has_table_privilege()), only on the sanctioned
#      ai_read_cash_transactions view -- rewritten to query the view.
#      modules/ai_console/live_adapters.py's payroll_page_summary (BUS-017)
#      had a related but separate bug: silently skipped the transactions
#      query entirely for relative-date phrases ("গতকাল"/yesterday) with no
#      explicit month/year, producing a confidently WRONG "0 payments"
#      answer -- fixed to fall back to date_from/date_to via the same
#      parse_date_range() helper, but ONLY when a real date phrase is
#      recognized (default_days=None), not for genuinely unscoped questions.
# All three verified against REAL production data (not just mocks) during
# the investigation -- see management_decisions.md for the full trace and
# exact before/after numbers. Remove this manifest block and commit
# together with the rest once the Owner confirms the re-verified live test
# passes.
